 What that buys, none of it authored:
 
@@ -663,7 +666,8 @@ The kernel depends only on the pupil's **shape**, so it is rebuilt on a **job**
 on the render thread, one in flight, the previous kernel stays live meanwhile) and only when
 blades, the polygon exponent, either rotation, the mask, the mask scale or the spherical
 aberration actually change. The f-number does **not** trigger a rebuild; it only scales the
-result. Each rebuild logs its parameters, the core fraction and the job's time.
+result. Each rebuild logs its parameters, the core fraction, the physical glare fraction
+(`1 - core`) and the job's time; the glare pass logs the fraction it actually deposits.
 
 Known limits: the pupil is the **on-axis** one, so the corners do not get their cat-eye-clipped
 stars; the convolution is shift-invariant; and a shape change takes a frame or two to appear.
diff --git a/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/HDRPostProcess.cfx b/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/HDRPostProcess.cfx
